# Override the stock ColorOS face-unlock HIDL service (face_hal).
#
# The stock service registers vendor.oppo.hardware.biometrics.face@1.0, which
# the AOSP/LineageOS 10 framework does not bind to directly: the source-built
# android.hardware.biometrics.face@1.0-service (biometrics/face/) is the AOSP
# interface the Lineage stack binds to, and it forwards to this backend through
# OppoFaceHal. Enable the backend so that forwarding path has a live peer:
#   - android.frameworks.faceservice@1.0.so is shipped into /vendor/lib{,64}
#     (LineageOS 17.1 does not build that interface), so the loader can start
#     the service.
#   - vendor.oppo.hardware.biometrics.face@1.0.so is built from source here.
# The ColorOS IFaceHalService handshake it calls is best-effort on stock; if
# the framework service is absent the backend still registers its own HAL.
service face_hal /vendor/bin/hw/vendor.oppo.hardware.biometrics.face@1.0-service
    override
    class late_start
    user system
    group system input
    oneshot
